<title>USA: U.S. 9-yr, 11-mo note auction average 6.273 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 9-yr, 11-mo note auction average 6.273 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its auction of 9-year, 11-month notes produced these results:</p>
<p>		     9-YEAR, 11-MONTH NOTES DUE OCT 15, 2006</p>
<p>			     $10.002 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> LOW	 6.260    Awarded At	101.739     6-1/2</p>
<p> HIGH	6.283    High Yield	101.570    Percent</p>
<p> AVERAGE   6.273    46 Percent	101.643</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.41 Times</p>
<p>	   Tail -- (High Minus Average Yield) =  1   Basis Pt</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 15.Oct.06</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    9 YEARS, 11 MONTHS	   PAY DATE 15.Nov.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 06.Nov.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  10.002 BLN USD		 CUSIP    912827Z62</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   24.061			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   306.00 MLN			AUCTION AVERAGES</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.500</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  0.00 MLN			 PRICE	101.643</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.283-6.260 PCT		YIELD	  6.273</p>
<p>AVERAGE YIELD DOWN FROM 6.502 PCT AT AUCTION ON 08.OCT.96 AVG YIELD LOWEST SINCE 5.649 PCT AT AUCTION ON 07.FEB.96</p>
</text>
